    at an `icon:` or a `logo:` node and live ENTIRELY inside the generated node
    file (knowledge/_icon_nodes.json / _logo_nodes.json), exactly as `tensionWith`
    and `hasParty` live inside _ux_principle_nodes.json. No meta ever carries one,
    so they need NOTHING in meta.schema.json. They need only the REF_RE /
    NODE_KINDS addition so `_validate_kg.py` can parse the ids at all.

  · TWO of the six — usesIcon and usesLogo — are sourced at a `component:` node.
    Those are the two a meta could hold, so those are the two that get a scoped
    definition and an `edges` field. They are GENERATED, not authored, which is
